led down so as not to burn your hands etc.","bullet":"black","level":0,"lineid":null,"text_rendered":"Again, looking at the left side (driver side) of the engine. As you can see, you are working right by the exhaust manifold. Make sure that your engine has sufficiently cooled down so as not to burn your hands etc."},{"text_raw":"Pull the first spark plug boot off the plug. Sometimes those are pretty tight on the plug. You can use a pair of pliers to remove the boot. Just make sure you don't tear the boot. If so, you'll need to replace the wires.","bullet":"black","level":0,"lineid":null,"text_rendered":"Pull the first spark plug boot off the plug. Sometimes those are pretty tight on the plug. You can use a pair of pliers to remove the boot. Just make sure you don't tear the boot. If so, you'll need to replace the wires."}],"guideid":107723,"stepid":206657,"orderby":2,"revisionid":3144327,"pending_patrol":{"gsr":null,"gst":null},"media":{"type":"image","data":[{"id":1440657,"guid":"ULefxKFLCL42CjYA","mini":"https:\/\/guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com\/igi\/ULefxKFLCL42CjYA.mini","thumbnail":"https:\/\/guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com\/igi\/ULefxKFLCL42CjYA.thumbnail","140x105":"https:\/\/guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com\/igi\/ULefxKFLCL42CjYA.140x105","200x150":"https:\/\/guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com\/igi\/ULefxKFLCL42CjYA.200x150","standard":"https:\/\/guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com\/igi\/ULefxKFLCL42CjYA.standard","440x330":"https:\/\/guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com\/igi\/ULefxKFLCL42CjYA.440x330","medium":"https:\/\/guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com\/igi\/ULefxKFLCL42CjYA.medium","large":"https:\/\/guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com\/igi\/ULefxKFLCL42CjYA.large","huge":"https:\/\/guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com\/igi\/ULefxKFLCL42CjYA.huge","original":"https:\/\/guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com\/igi\/ULefxKFLCL42CjYA.full"},{"id":3015813,"guid":"IQgpiMwRCELDsFjm","mini":"https:\/\/guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com\/igi\/IQgpiMwRCELDsFjm.mini","thumbnail":"https:\/\/guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com\/igi\/IQgpiMwRCELDsFjm.